# Installed-name globs LEFT OUT of the full variant (everything else in linux-firmware's WHENCE is included). Globs match the
# whole installed path, "*" crosses "/". "@latest N GLOB" keeps only the N highest -<number> versions per family.
# Reasons: no driver for it in this kernel, ARM/embedded SoC only, audio/camera/video-codec blocks, or dead weight.
# Policy for GPUs: amdgpu, i915, xe and nvidia (nouveau GSP) STAY: without their firmware a loaded GPU driver cannot finish its
# probe and would take the console away from simpledrm.
# --- ARM / embedded SoC and phone-class blobs (the single largest block: Qualcomm SoC DSP/GPU/video)
qcom/*
ti/*
ti-connectivity/*
imx/*
amlogic/*
amphion/*
arm/*
cnm/*
cadence/*
dpaa2/*
mediatek/mt8*
mediatek/mt7986*
mediatek/mt7988*
airoha/*
# --- NICs/switches whose driver we do not build (their firmware lives on the card or the part is a switch ASIC)
netronome/*
mellanox/*
mrvl/prestera/*
liquidio/*
cavium/*
cxgb3/*
cxgb4/*
qlogic/*
ql2*
hfi1_*
# --- audio, camera, video codecs, TV tuners (CONFIG_SOUND is off; no media stack)
intel/avs/*
intel/catpt/*
intel/sof*
intel/dsp_fw*
intel/fw_sst*
intel/ipu/*
intel/vpu/*
intel/vsc/*
intel/qat/*
cirrus/*
dvb*
av7110/*
go7007/*
cpia2/*
v4l-*
cx*
as102*
cmmb*
ctefx.bin
ctspeq.bin
ctfw*
cs42l43.bin
sb16/*
yamaha/*
korg/*
emu/*
ess/*
# --- old Intel Wi-Fi API versions: keep the newest 2 per family (kernels ask for the newest they know, then fall back)
@latest 2 *iwlwifi-*.ucode
